            "id": "p38-q11-response",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "",
            "prompt": "Find the width and height of the rectangle which will give the greatest possible area of the cross-section.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$w=20\\text{ cm},\\ h=10\\text{ cm}$.",
              "worked": "The maximum occurs halfway between the intercepts, by symmetry of the parabola.\n$$\\begin{align*}w&=\\frac{0+40}{2}=20\\text{ cm}\\\\A&=-0.5(20)^2+20(20)\\\\A&=200\\text{ cm}^{2}\\end{align*}$$\nSince the rectangle has area $A=wh$,\n$$\\begin{align*}h&=\\frac{A}{w}\\\\h&=\\frac{200}{20}=10\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, the width is $20\\text{ cm}$ and the height is $10\\text{ cm}$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 45
          }
        ]
